{"title":"1974 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 16th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1974 in East Germany. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> play the following game: On each of three cards an integer is written. These three numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689d638ddca59030006d362cbd848607f63aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28359ee7a048e91f97f732bd96e99d124e49dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; p &lt; q &lt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />. The three cards are shuffled and one is dealt to each player. Each then receives the number of counters indicated by the card he holds. Then the cards are shuffled again; the counters remain with the players.\n</p><p>This process (shuffling, dealing, giving out counters) takes place for at least two rounds. After the last round, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has 20 counters in all, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has 10 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has 9. At the last round <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> received <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> counters. Who received <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> counters on the first round?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, prove that there is a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is the geometric mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b263ec4c2e1e4a9f4cf0c1de3514be34379d203.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{A} \\sin{B} \\leq \\sin^2 \\frac{C}{2}.\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aae582fb5f5ac10995f2e68050a9c65971a2064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\sum_{k = 0}^n \\tbinom{2n+1}{2k+1} 2^{3k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"117\" height=\"23\" /> is not divisible by 5 for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider decompositions of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bb73e4f0a880ad6bdaf6948c771579951be92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> chessboard into p non-overlapping rectangles subject to the following conditions:\n</p><p>(i) Each rectangle has as many white squares as black squares.\n</p><p>(ii) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of white squares in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />-th rectangle, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e46963c9b266a9e28e41d118e1fcedea5b9d094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Find the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for which such a decomposition is possible. For this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, determine all possible sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bca295f334ba985ec48a334a48c6d6fc751eeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all possible values of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c1725ef98d8c9540e019687d7f566ebe3e6e6fb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{a}{a+b+d} + \\frac{b}{a+b+c} + \\frac{c}{b+c+d} + \\frac{d}{a+c+d}\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"39\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are arbitrary positive numbers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a non-constant polynomial with integer coefficients. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a278cb7eaae574a083567eec2cba75b332da4701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is the number of distinct integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede4ae2ccb270263a109aeb1a018fdb1b05b92cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P(k))^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" />, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/73651c97b1badcdc472066849efa52ee431c5aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(P) - \\deg(P) \\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc3bca75e183256c55ff7ea50b2a7d9e150a3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the degree of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO\" title=\"1974 IMO\">1974 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1974\">IMO 1974 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO\" title=\"1974 IMO\">1974 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO\" title=\"1973 IMO\">1973 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO\" title=\"1975 IMO\">1975 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202819\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 206/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6212/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.605      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.605      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8943:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202819 and revision id 143893. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}